From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:22:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a theme style the on-screen keyboard and show its focus

The on-screen keyboard opened on its text field, which a pad cannot
type into, so no key showed the focus, and the caret was dimmed or
blinked away. Its keys were drawn with the stock button images, a
tiny check for accept and a blank space bar.

A theme can now give the keys their own look with a menuKeyboard
element: images for a key, the focused key and a toggled SHIFT or
ALT (drawn untinted), the spacing between keys, the label font and
colours, words instead of glyphs for delete, space and accept, and
opening on the first letter key. menuTextEdit gains a font and a
caret colour, kept at full strength while the keys type into the
field. Without these properties the keyboard is unchanged.
